# ImGui Module

## Purpose

Shell and tool UI via Dear ImGui. Lives outside graphics so the render backend stays toolkit-agnostic. Game presentation uses `PresentPass`; ImGui is an optional overlay (debug) or the full UI surface (AnimTool).

## Layout

```
src/core/imgui/
  vendor/                 # Upstream Dear ImGui only -- do not mix engine code here
    imgui.h / imgui.cpp / backends / misc/
  ImGuiRenderPass.h/.cpp  # Swapchain overlay pass (eage::imgui)
  ImGUILifetime.h/.cpp    # Context + SDL2/Vulkan backend init
```

## Includes

| What | Include |
|---|---|
| Engine wrappers | `#include <imgui/ImGuiRenderPass.h>` |
| Dear ImGui | `#include <imgui/vendor/imgui.h>` (and `imgui_impl_*`) |

## Key Classes

| Class | Namespace | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `ImGUILifetime` | `eage::imgui` | Creates ImGui context; inits SDL2 + Vulkan backends; owns descriptor pool |
| `ImGuiRenderPass` | `eage::imgui` | `AbstractRenderPass` that records ImGui draw data to the swapchain |

## Dependencies

```
apps / tools / profiling
        |
        v
   eage::imgui  (wrappers)
        |
        +---> graphics (AbstractRenderPass, ManagedImage, VulkanContext)
        |
        +---> imgui/vendor (Dear ImGui)
```

Graphics must never include or link this module.

## Usage

```cpp
// Game shell: overlay on PresentPass (no clear)
auto imgui = std::make_unique<eage::imgui::ImGuiRenderPass>( ... );
imgui->SetClearColor( std::nullopt );
imgui->AddOverlayCallback( [&]{ tracker.DrawDebugGUI(); } );

// AnimTool: clears swapchain and samples scene for preview panels
imgui->SetSceneInput( &scene_pass->GetColorTarget() );
```

## DOs

- Keep vendor/ free of engine code; update Dear ImGui by replacing vendor contents only
- Register `ImGuiRenderPass` via `Renderer::AddRenderPass` from the shell/tool -- graphics does not own it
- Use `SetClearColor( nullopt )` when compositing on top of `PresentPass`

## DON'Ts

- Don't put ImGui code back under `graphics/`
- Don't depend on `game/` from this module
- Don't include `<imgui/imgui.h>` -- use `<imgui/vendor/imgui.h>`
- Don't have graphics include imgui wrappers
